Z||000000||Hym-The-Man||05-24-2001||06:16 PM||||Has anyone tried using the emc from a Chevrolet caprice without traction control and all of that sh#t?  It has the v8 and probably most of the sensors that the orthstar has, but it would sefinately be less sophisticated.  This is just a theory, but if anyone could help put I am sure that there will be alot of people interested in that.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||05-24-2001||06:20 PM||||The Chip in a caprice is based on a 486 processor , and does not monitor nearly the number of sensors the Northstar does.<P>I heard this from a friend who runs the one lap of america<P>The internals of a Northstar computer are Motorola Based if I remember correctly.<P><BR>I think you would cause more problems than you would solve. There are a few people out there working on this problem. Chris Moore is Working With Lingenfelter Performance enginnering on solving the problem. If anyone figures it out , it will be them.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||05-24-2001||06:39 PM||||Never thought of that or know enough about it.  Chris is the man on this one, I'm waiting for his chip to be tested and dynoed.  I think the only way of getting it right is to do something custom.  I don't have the knowledge of chips and programming needed and Design One has been lax in returning my requests for a chip.  I also have some leads on others persuing this cause, but I think that Chris is our best bet!  Never met him, just through talking on the forum, but I think he knows his stuff!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
